# THE JOURNAL ARCHIVE (scripts/journal.py, data/journal_archive/): one file per
# month of what the live journal pruned.
# A sealed month is gzip, written once and never changed: never diffed, never
# merged as text, never touched by line-ending conversion. Two seals of one
# month that came out differently, or a month sealed on one side and appended
# to on the other, are settled by row (journal.py --resolve; merge_decisions.py
# --resolve in the workflows), never by picking a side's bytes.
data/journal_archive/*.gz binary
# The open months are plain JSON lines, deliberately WITHOUT merge=union: a
# merge from a branch older than the migration follows the old single file
# into a month file git judges a rename of it, and a union there would append
# other months' rows - and the old file's tail - to it without a word. Two
# appends to one month stop instead, and are settled by row as above.
